Elite Dangerous game data
-------------------------

Directive 47 was created using assets and imagery from Elite Dangerous, with the
permission of Frontier Developments plc, for non-commercial purposes. It is not
endorsed by nor reflects the views or opinions of Frontier Developments and no
employee of Frontier Developments was involved in the making of it.

That is Frontier's own long-form attribution, from the Elite Dangerous Media Usage
Rules:

    https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/elite-dangerous-media-usage-rules.510879/

Those rules permit non-commercial community projects to use Frontier's game content
provided it is clearly attributed, and require written permission for commercial use.
**Directive 47 is non-commercial.** The MIT licence above covers the code; it is not
a grant of any right over Frontier's game data, and anyone reusing this project is
bound by Frontier's rules independently of it.

The following shipped tables contain game data derived under those rules. Each is
generated by a script in tools/, never hand-written, and each records the source it
was derived from in its own header:

    src/D47.Core/Journal/MaterialGrades.g.cs        tools/gen-material-grades.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/EliteSpecifications.tsv  tools/gen-elite-specs.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Engineers.tsv            tools/gen-engineers.py


Community data sources
----------------------

These supply the ids, names and figures the generators above join together. Their own
licences are recorded here; none of them conveys rights over the underlying game data,
which remains Frontier's in every case.

    EDCD/FDevIDs           No licence file. The canonical community id list, and the
                           source of the symbols the journal writes.

    EDCD/coriolis-data     Code MIT. Its LICENSE.md states that the data and JSON
                           files are the intellectual property of Frontier
                           Developments plc.

    msarilar/EDEngineer    MIT.

    taleden/EDSY           Code CC BY-NC 4.0. Its header states that the Elite
                           Dangerous game logic and data in the file remain the
                           property of Frontier Developments plc, used under the same
                           Media Usage Rules quoted above. It is the source of the
                           per-hull slot layout — what the journal calls a slot before
                           anything is fitted to it — which neither source above
                           carries.

Sources examined and deliberately not used are recorded, with the reasons, in
docs/spikes/README.md.


